# A .gitignore for backing up ~/.claude to a PRIVATE git repo.
#
# Kit note: later shelf. The moment for it: the two-week check-in, if anything you built
# has survived. After a month or two your harness is irreplaceable, and one bad edit or a
# dead laptop loses it. Copy this file to ~/.claude/.gitignore, then `git init` there and
# push to a PRIVATE repository.
#
# Before the FIRST push: run `git status` and read every file it lists. An early backup of
# the harness this kit comes from pushed a login token that then had to be scrubbed from
# the repo's history. Check settings.json too: an MCP server's API key can live in it.
#
# What's kept: CLAUDE.md, rules, skills, commands, hooks, settings, and each project's
# memory folder (the hand-built, irreplaceable part). What's dropped: caches, logs, and
# session transcripts (large and machine-specific; if you want them kept, see the
# cleanupPeriodDays setting instead).

# --- Secrets: never version these ---
.credentials.json
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*

# --- Regenerable or machine-local ---
cache/
paste-cache/
shell-snapshots/
sessions/
debug/
backups/
telemetry/
tasks/
session-env/
plugins/
todos/
history.jsonl
stats-cache.json
*.log
node_modules/
*.bak

# --- Hook runtime state (keep the scripts, drop what they write) ---
hooks/state/

# --- Projects: drop everything EXCEPT each project's memory folder ---
/projects/*
!/projects/*/
/projects/*/*
!/projects/*/memory/

# --- OS / editor noise ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
